hog: queue mouse reports without waiting

The pointing input listener sends one mouse report per input event, from
the system work queue, and zmk_hog_send_mouse_report() waited up to 100 ms
for room in the HOG queue on each. While the Bluetooth link stalls, the
queue stays full: with a pointing device sending 80-100 events a second the
listener never catches up, and the system work queue runs nothing else
until the link drops. A watchdog fed from the work queue then resets the
board if the stall lasts long enough.

Queue without waiting and drop the oldest report when the queue is full,
as before after the wait. Every report carries the present buttons, so what
is lost is movement over a link that isn't delivering it anyway. The
message, which said "Consumer" and could now come 100 times a second, is
debug level.

Applies to petejohanson/zmk 5565f21; the earlier patches don't touch
hog.c.

diff --git a/app/src/hog.c b/app/src/hog.c
index 32a5c73..288c513 100644
--- a/app/src/hog.c
+++ b/app/src/hog.c
@@ -448,11 +448,14 @@ void send_mouse_report_callback(struct k_work *work) {
 K_WORK_DEFINE(hog_mouse_work, send_mouse_report_callback);
 
 int zmk_hog_send_mouse_report(struct zmk_hid_mouse_report_body *report) {
-    int err = k_msgq_put(&zmk_hog_mouse_msgq, report, K_MSEC(100));
+    // No waiting: the pointing input listener calls this from the system work
+    // queue for every event. A stalled link would otherwise hold the queue
+    // there 100 ms per report, for as long as the device keeps moving.
+    int err = k_msgq_put(&zmk_hog_mouse_msgq, report, K_NO_WAIT);
     if (err) {
         switch (err) {
-        case -EAGAIN: {
-            LOG_WRN("Consumer message queue full, popping first message and queueing again");
+        case -ENOMSG: {
+            LOG_DBG("Mouse message queue full, dropping the oldest report");
             struct zmk_hid_mouse_report_body discarded_report;
             k_msgq_get(&zmk_hog_mouse_msgq, &discarded_report, K_NO_WAIT);
             return zmk_hog_send_mouse_report(report);
